{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContentDichotomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContentDichotomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboIdentity","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.DecupletEqualSpacing"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decuplet_has_content_nonet_does_not","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decuplet_has_content_nonet_does_not","kind":"theorem","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L311-L317","doc":"**The contrast, in one statement.**  Within the same chapter: the decuplet\nansatz has content and the nonet ansatz does not.  This is the dichotomy doing\nthe work it was written for — telling apart two ansätze that both look like\n\"a linear mass formula with a few parameters\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz_not_unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz_not_unconstraining","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L307-L309","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz_discriminating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz_discriminating","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L300-L305","doc":"**So the decuplet ansatz is discriminating too** — Gell-Mann's `Ω`\nextrapolation is a falsifiable claim about the four masses, even though it\nextracts no information about which mechanism produced them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletRel_not_vacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletRel_not_vacuous","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L291-L298","doc":"Equal spacing is not vacuous: `(0, 0, 0, 1)` violates it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz_forces_decupletRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz_forces_decupletRel","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L282-L289","doc":"The ansatz forces equal spacing — `second_difference_vanishes` restated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletRel","kind":"def","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L277-L279","doc":"The equal-spacing relation as a `Rel`: the second difference\n`(Ω − Ξ*) − (Ξ* − Σ*)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.decupletAnsatz","kind":"def","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L271-L275","doc":"The decuplet ansatz: the same three breaking parameters to the four decuplet\nmasses `(Δ, Σ*, Ξ*, Ω)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_not_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_not_injective","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L251-L268","doc":"**And the other sense, separately.**  The ansatz map is not injective — the\nbreaking strength `b` is invisible to all three GMO observables, since the pion\nand eta sit at `Y = 0` and the two kaon hypercharges cancel in the average.\n`(0,0,0)` and `(0,1,0)` are different mechanisms with identical observables.\n\nThis is `gmo_independent_of_breaking_strength` as a statement about the map, and\nit is what *\"cannot discriminate\"* means in the source file — a different claim\nfrom `Discriminating` above, and compatible with it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmo_exists_unreachable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmo_exists_unreachable","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L243-L248","doc":"The operational form: some measurement is out of the ansatz's reach, i.e.\nGMO names a triple of meson masses that would falsify first-order octet\nbreaking. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_not_unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_not_unconstraining","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L239-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_discriminating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_discriminating","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L232-L237","doc":"**Therefore GMO is a discriminating relation**, and by\n`not_unconstraining_of_discriminating` the first-order octet ansatz is *not*\nunconstraining. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoRel_not_vacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoRel_not_vacuous","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L222-L230","doc":"But GMO is **not** vacuous: the observable triple `(1, 0, 0)` violates it.\nSo the relation does say something about the observables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_forces_gmoRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz_forces_gmoRel","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L212-L220","doc":"The ansatz forces GMO — this is `gmo_combination_vanishes` restated in the\ndichotomy's vocabulary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoRel","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L208-L209","doc":"The Gell-Mann–Okubo combination `4m²_K − 3m²_η − m²_π`, as a `Rel`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.gmoAnsatz","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L200-L206","doc":"The first-order `SU(3)`-breaking ansatz of `GellMannOkuboIdentity` as an\n`Ansatz`: the three breaking parameters `(a, b, c)` to the three observables\nGMO is stated on, `(4m²_π, 4m²_η, 2·(4m²_K))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz_not_unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz_not_unconstraining","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L157-L161","doc":"And therefore it is **not** unconstraining: some observation refutes it.\nThis is the case the eightfold-way ansätze are *not* in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz_discriminating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz_discriminating","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L148-L155","doc":"Over a nontrivial ring the relation is **not** vacuous — `(0, 1)` violates\nit — so `equalPairAnsatz` genuinely discriminates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz_forces_diffRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz_forces_diffRel","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L144-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.diffRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.diffRel","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L141-L142","doc":"The relation \"the two observables agree\", as a `Rel`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.equalPairAnsatz","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L136-L139","doc":"A **restrictive** ansatz, exhibited so that the hypothesis of the dichotomy\nis not vacuously satisfiable: the model that predicts two equal observables.\nIt has one parameter and two observables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.nonet_no_discriminating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.nonet_no_discriminating","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L127-L130","doc":"Consequently no relation among the nonet's two coefficients discriminates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.nonetAnsatz_unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.nonetAnsatz_unconstraining","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**`mixing_unconstrained` is an instance of this dichotomy.**  The nonet\nansatz is surjective onto the coefficient plane, so by\n`not_discriminating_of_unconstraining` it admits no testable prediction about\nwhere the physical states sit or how strongly they mix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.nonetAnsatz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.nonetAnsatz","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L110-L115","doc":"The nonet coefficient map of `NonetMixingUnconstrained`, as an `Ansatz`: the\nfree parameters are the singlet diagonal entry `d₂` and the squared mixing\n`esq`, and the observables are the two characteristic-polynomial coefficients\n(trace and determinant) with the octet entry `d₁` held fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.exists_unreachable_of_discriminating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.exists_unreachable_of_discriminating","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L97-L106","doc":"Explicitly: a discriminating relation exhibits an **unreachable**\nobservation.  This is the operational content — it names the measurement that\nwould falsify the model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.not_unconstraining_of_discriminating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.not_unconstraining_of_discriminating","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L87-L95","doc":"**The usable direction (contrapositive).**  A genuine prediction certifies\nthat the ansatz is restrictive.\n\nIf a model forces a relation that is *not* true of every observable tuple, then\nsome observable tuple is out of its reach — so the model has content, and the\nmeasurement is capable of refuting it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.not_discriminating_of_unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.not_discriminating_of_unconstraining","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L80-L85","doc":"**No discriminating relation survives an unconstraining ansatz.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.vacuous_of_forces_of_unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.vacuous_of_forces_of_unconstraining","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L67-L78","doc":"**The dichotomy.**  An unconstraining ansatz forces only vacuous relations.\n\nThis is the general form of the contrast drawn in `NonetMixingUnconstrained`:\n\"empty\" and \"vacuous\" are not two ways for an ansatz to fail, they are one.  If\nnothing can refute the model, then anything it appears to predict was already\ntrue of every conceivable measurement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Discriminating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Discriminating","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L62-L65","doc":"`rel` **discriminates** for `A`: the ansatz forces it, and it is not true\nanyway.  This is exactly what a testable prediction is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Unconstraining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Unconstraining","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L58-L60","doc":"`A` is **unconstraining**: every observable tuple is realised by some\nparameter choice.  No measurement can refute such an ansatz. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Forces","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L53-L56","doc":"`A` **forces** `rel`: every parameter choice produces observables satisfying\nit.  This is what \"the ansatz predicts the relation\" means. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Vacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Vacuous","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L48-L51","doc":"`rel` is **vacuous**: it holds of every observable tuple whatsoever.  A\nvacuous relation is not evidence for any ansatz, because it is not evidence for\nanything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Ansatz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Ansatz","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L45-L46","doc":"An **ansatz**: a model carrying `p` parameters to the `n` observables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Rel","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L41-L43","doc":"A **relation** among observables, tested by asking whether `rel obs = 0`.\nGell-Mann–Okubo and decuplet equal spacing are both of this shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Obs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.AnsatzContent.Obs","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/AnsatzContentDichotomy.lean#L37-L39","doc":"An **observable tuple**: the `n` numbers a measurement reports (masses of a\nmultiplet, say). ","signatureChunk":0}]}